messages:
emma_support: Customer reports TS SDK JSON streaming parser fails with 'Unexpected token' when JSON objects are split across chunks. Happens with streaming:true + json:true. Customer sees parser errors intermittently and app crashes.
rahul_eng: Can you paste a minimal repro or raw chunks? Sounds like NDJSON vs JSON-stream mismatch.
liza_engineer: Also need to confirm SDK version and whether they use the high-level responses.stream helper or raw fetch. Small differences there.
emma_support: Repro steps from user (simplified):
1) call responses.stream with { model: 'redwood-1', json: true, stream: true }
2) client collects chunks and does buffer += chunk
3) try JSON.parse(buffer) after each chunk -> throws when a chunk boundary splits a string or object
Code they ran:
```ts
const stream = client.responses.stream({ model: 'redwood-1', json: true, stream: true });
let buf = '';
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  buf += chunk;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    handle(obj);
    buf = '';
  } catch (e) {
    // user expects to wait for more data
  }
}
```
rahul_eng: That pattern is racy for any streaming transport unless you emit NDJSON (one JSON object per line). If the runtime sometimes sends partial objects (no newline delim) then JSON.parse will fail. Do they have a Content-Type or delimiter?
liza_engineer: Recent runtime deploy changed chunking heuristics (more aggressive kernel-level flushing). Previously most responses ended up as line-delimited objects; now you can get object fragments. We didn't update SDK docs to require an incremental parser.
emma_support: Customer says they used SDK v0.6.1. They expected to get complete JSON objects per chunk.
rahul_eng: Interim workarounds:
- Switch to NDJSON mode if available (Accept: application/x-ndjson or use json_lines:true) so each object ends with \n and you can parse per-line.
- Use a streaming JSON parser (clarinet, oboe, JSONStream) instead of buffer+JSON.parse.
- Buffer until a heuristic indicates completeness: e.g., only try JSON.parse when buffer.trim().endsWith('}') and counts of '{' and '}' match. Not bulletproof but helps.
liza_engineer: Action items: collect the raw chunk sequence (base64) + SDK logs + runtime chunk boundaries. We need to reproduce with v0.6.1 and latest runtime (deploy-bot just rolled v2.14.7).
deploy-bot: Deployed redwood-runtime v2.14.7 @ 1770204700 — note: improved latency batching, changed flush thresholds.
rahul_eng: I'll spin up a local harness to emulate smaller chunk sizes and confirm. If we confirm, patch options: 1) SDK implement incremental JSON parser and fallback, 2) runtime add configurable per-connection delimiter mode, 3) docs update.
emma_support: User asked for ETA for a fix; they are in production.
rahul_eng: Short-term ETA: post a documented workaround in 2-6 hrs. Medium: SDK hotfix with defensive parsing 24-36 hrs. Runtime change requires rollout so longer. I'm opening internal ticket SR-3492 and will attach traces.
liza_engineer: I'll add a note to the release board and tag platform security to review any header changes.
emma_support: I'll send the workaround to the customer (NDJSON + streaming parser + heuristic) and request the raw chunk logs. Thanks all. :pray:
